---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Install and connect">
  <h1>Put the dashboard beside your Mac</h1>
  <section class="card"><h2>1. Install on Android</h2><p>Use an Android 9 or later tablet. Download the APK from the <a href={`${base}/releases/`}>beta release</a>, allow installation from that download source, then open Codex Micro Tablet. The app starts in landscape, in either cable direction.</p><p>The APK is debug-signed. Updating an existing install requires the same signing certificate. A different certificate requires uninstalling the old app, which removes its saved settings.</p></section>
  <section class="card"><h2>2. Connect with Bluetooth LE</h2><ol><li>Open Connection settings, select BLE and tap <strong>Start BLE HID</strong>.</li><li>On your Mac, pair with <strong>Codex Micro Tablet</strong>, then open Codex’s Micro settings.</li><li>Wait for <strong>Micro linked</strong> before testing a harmless mapped action. Pairing alone does not confirm discovery.</li></ol><p>Keep the dashboard open. If a connected session stalls at discovery, disconnect/reconnect from the Mac and reopen Micro settings. In the observed case, turning Mac Bluetooth off and on restored discovery.</p></section>
  <section class="card"><h2>3. Add live quota and chats</h2><p>Run the existing <a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/tree/main/monitor-server" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FNK0104B monitor-server</a> on the Mac. Open the tablet’s bridge settings and enter the Mac’s LAN address and the same monitor key used by your ESP32. The Mac’s loopback address is not reachable from the tablet.</p><p>Tap a named chat and then <strong>Message</strong> to write to it, or leave the selection empty to start a new thread. Review approvals on the Mac.</p></section>
  <section class="card"><h2>Optional: rooted USB HID</h2><p>On the tested stock Lenovo TB-8505F, select USB HID, tap <strong>Start USB HID</strong> and allow the app in Magisk. Connect a data cable to the Mac. After moving the cable, use Start again if disconnected.</p><p><strong>Release controls / restore USB</strong> is available in the header and Connection settings. USB is experimental and device-specific. No kernel flashing is required by this app.</p></section>
  <section class="card"><h2>Build from source</h2><pre>git clone https://github.com/cmwen/codex-micro-tablet.git
cd codex-micro-tablet
flutter pub get
flutter analyze
flutter test
flutter build apk --debug</pre><p>The repository pins Flutter 3.38.7 and uses Java 17. Configure your private signing separately through <a href="https://github.com/cmwen/codex-micro-tablet/blob/main/SIGNING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SIGNING.md</a> for production builds.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
